go-to: root

A courier takes a copy to Radek, who has been the party's friend in the Comintern and Trotsky's in the Politburo. It is put in the right hands within a week. Radek reads it twice and says only that it must be used at the right time, and not by him.

Within days the Left Opposition in Moscow has a weapon. The balance in the Russian party tips against the secretaries, and the drift that had been carrying it toward Stalin stops. Nothing is decided yet; the Central Committee has not met. Our own Left, which takes the credit, grows by twelve points of strength, and Brandler's wing does not forgive us for having thrown a lighted match into the Russian party without asking it first.

@right
