go-to: root

Brandler's channel runs through Bukharin, who is the Right's friend and the party's theorist, and through Rykov and Tomsky, who run the state and the trade unions. They have their own reasons not to want a Secretariat that governs the party by its appointments, and a dead man's opinion is useful to them.

The balance in the Russian party slides against the secretaries, and its drift toward Stalin stops. Nothing is decided yet; the Central Committee has not met. Our own Right gains twelve points of strength, because it can now claim the friendship of the men who will matter, and the Left, which would have used the paper for a different man, is angrier by ten.

@publish
subtitle: A public break. Trust −20, Stalin loses ground, both oppositions gain. Left and Right +6 strength, Centre −10 strength and +10 dissent.
