go-to: root

Extracts go to the party's press on a Sunday, under a headline that does not name the man they are about. By Monday the other papers have them as well, and the SPD's Vorwärts prints them next to an article about the dictatorship inside the Russian party. The men whose names are on the paper read it in the German papers.

The Centre, loyal to the secretariat that has been loyal to it, is dismayed, and loses ten points of strength and gains ten of dissent. Both oppositions, in Berlin as in Moscow, take heart, and the balance in the Russian party moves against the secretaries, though nothing is decided before the Central Committee meets. Moscow does not take it quietly, and our standing with the Comintern falls by twenty.

@hold
subtitle: Trust +5, Centre +2 strength. The paper stays in reserve.
